   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Robin Built a Nest On Daddy's Grave**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **I Believe In You Darling**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Lonesome River**: back after 197 archived shows (992 days); rare: 11 archived performances [2]\n- **Train on the Island**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2020-09-18.oktava.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 130 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Ian Goldberg [1]\n- The show was part of the Meet Me at the Drive-In Tour, played in two sets plus an encore [1]\n- Exposition Gardens hosts The Heart of Illinois Fair [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2020-09-18.oktava.flac16**: taped by Michael Frasca; transferred by Michael Frasca; source: Audience, left of soundboard, 120 feet from stage, MJE-modified Oktava MK-012 cardioids in an A-B pattern with 10cm of spread-> Tascam DR-40-> wav @44.1K-> SD… [1]. Also: Recorded with Oktava microphones from the 4th row of the Silver Section, four cars left of the soundboard [1]",
